# 2026-07-30 implementation notes
- Much of D2's runtime behavior had already converged via prior work:
  the five named snippets (s045/s090/s094/s123/s168), *peek(v) and
  *bsort(v) all compiled — but via the i64-defaulting path, with
  spurious repeated warnings whose fix-it (`: i64`) the parser rejects.
  Monomorphization DID specialize correctly per call site; the noise
  came from the definition-site pre-pass whose HIR is discarded.
- Fixed: unsolved-variable reports (warnings AND strict errors) are
  suppressed during the inferable-generic pre-pass
  (InferCtx.suppress_unsolved_reports, set in lower_fn) — definition-
  site typing is deferred to instantiation, D2's accepted tradeoff.
  Real ambiguity resurfaces when the mono body is lowered with concrete
  types. This is what makes `*peek(v)` strict-clean.
- Soundness holes closed: occurs_in / resolve_core / canonicalize_type
  now recurse into Struct(_, args) and Alias/Newtype (`?v ~
  Struct(n,[?v])` used to pass occurs; Struct args escaped resolution
  via the identity arm). The Struct(n,args) ↔ Enum(n) shim now touches
  each arg (recording usage sites) instead of silently dropping them.
- All fix-it texts use valid Jinn: `as i64`, never `: i64`.
- Warnings deduped at drain (same origin resolved across passes).
- Exported-generic rule: a --lib ARTIFACT build errors for an inferable
  generic with no call site in the unit (it would be silently dropped
  from the object); --emit-hir/--emit-llvm/--emit-interface are exempt —
  modules distribute as source and instantiate at user call sites (the
  std model), so the std frontend gate stays green.
- Deviation noted: the full audit of ~25 unwrap_or(Type::I64) sites was
  scoped to the flagged pattern (default-plus-strict-double-report,
  fix-it validity, Struct-arg escape). The remaining literal
  unwrap_or(I64) sites are follow-up hygiene.
- tests/generic_args.rs: peek/bsort zero-annotation clean-run, String
  element stays String, mixed instantiations in one program, lib
  diagnostic, fix-it validity.
